Header template. See https://pptr.dev/api/puppeteer.pdfoptions -> headerTemplate for info.

Use one of the following puppeteer variables to include dynamic content:

<span class="pageNumber"></span>  -> current page number
<span class="totalPages"></span>  -> total number of pages
<span class="date"></span>  -> current date
<span class="title"></span>  -> document title
<span class="url"></span>  -> document URL

Also, you can use the following handlebars variables:
- metadata: the OpenAPI metadata object

NOTE1: Set the style directly in this file, do not use external styles.css.
NOTE2: Be sure to set text size in pixels, or text may not appear in the PDF.
NOTE3: If you don't want a header, leave this file empty or add a minimal, empty div/span
Example:

<div style="font-size: 13px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; width: 100%; padding: 0 10px;">
    <span>{{metadata.title}}</span>
    <span class="pageNumber"></span>
</div>


